==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|hōh|lang=goh}}, {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*hauhaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*kewk-}}, a suffixed form of {{term/t|ine-pro|*kew-}}. Compare Dutch {{term|hoog|lang=nl}}, English {{term|high|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|høj|lang=da}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[hoːx]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-hoch.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|De-at-hoch.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

===Adjective===
{{de-adj|höher|höchsten}}

# [[high]], [[tall]]
# [[large]], [[big]], [[heavy]]
# [[grand]], [[important]]
# {{context|mathematics|lang=de}} [[to the power of]]
#: ''fünf '''hoch''' drei''
#:: five to the power of three

====Usage notes====
* As a predicative (after the verbs ''[[sein]]'' "be", ''[[werden]]'' "become" and ''[[bleiben]]'' "remain") the form '''hoch''' is used, but when declined, as an attribute, the form is '''hoh-'''.
: ''Der Preis ist '''hoch'''.'' — The price is high.
: '''''hoh'''e Preise'' — high prices

